|name = Otta-smack-u
|image = E 033.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Thriller Bridge|Sub-chapter 5 - Thriller Bridge]]<br>
'''ItF''': [[Machu Picchu (Into the Future)|Chapter 3 - Machu Picchu]]<br>
'''Aku Realms''': [[Singapore (Aku Realm)|Singapore/Ehime]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[So-So City Center|Sub-chapter 5 - So-So City Center]]
|money drop = 200¢ - 790¢
}}

==Enemy==
This enemy has one knockback, rapid attacks, short range, high stats and decent speed. Their money drop is unusually low, so using a lot of your budget to kill them can be risky, especially if spawned in groups.

At 100% strength magnification, Otta-smack-u has very similar stats to a 50% [[Dagshund]], but can push more easily with their shorter backswing.

==Strategy==
Large amounts of [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cats]] are good counters. Later on, when this enemy is buffed heavily, if they're not with a lot of support, you can use [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying Cat]] to inflict heavy damage, as the latter's short range is not much of a concern then. [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-controllers]] like [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]] and/or [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]] are good at halting them, and units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] or a stack of [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cats]] can also cripple them greatly.

